# Core Sources

## 1. David Kinsley — *Tantric Visions of the Divine Feminine*

[https://archive.org/search?query=%22Tantric+Visions+of+the+Divine+Feminine%22](https://archive.org/search?query=%22Tantric+Visions+of+the+Divine+Feminine%22)

Foundational English study of the ten Mahāvidyās, including Bagalāmukhī’s myths, imagery and association with *stambhana*. Copyrighted; use summary and brief quotation only.

## 2. *Śrī Bagalāmukhī Tattva Vimarśa*

[https://www.sanskrit.nic.in/books_archive/020_Shri_Bangalamukhi_Tatva_Vimarsha_of_Dr_Lakshimi_Narayana_Shastri.pdf](https://www.sanskrit.nic.in/books_archive/020_Shri_Bangalamukhi_Tatva_Vimarsha_of_Dr_Lakshimi_Narayana_Shastri.pdf)

Substantial modern Sanskrit/Hindi compendium. Useful for locating text names, myths and later theological interpretation; not automatically a critical historical edition. ([Central Sanskrit University][5])

## 3. *Brahmāstra Vidyā evaṃ Bagalāmukhī Sādhanā*

[https://archive.org/details/BrahamastraVidyaEvamBaglamukhiSadhanaShyamakantDwivediAnandChowkamabha_201811](https://archive.org/details/BrahamastraVidyaEvamBaglamukhiSadhanaShyamakantDwivediAnandChowkamabha_201811)

